<section class="section" id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="kicker">How it works</span>
      <h2>Four tool calls, the same four steps every time.</h2>
      <p>Marshal exposes a small set of MCP tools — connect, push, test, deploy — so any assistant gets the same predictable path from finished code to something running.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">01</div>
        <h3>Connect</h3>
        <p>Point Marshal at a repo and a deploy target once, in a single config file. Every assistant on the project shares that same connection.</p>
        <div class="call">marshal.connect(repo, target)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">02</div>
        <h3>Push</h3>
        <p>The assistant hands off finished code — Marshal commits it, opens a PR or pushes straight to a branch, per your config.</p>
        <div class="call">marshal.push_code(files, branch)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">03</div>
        <h3>Test</h3>
        <p>Your real test command runs in an isolated runner. Results — pass, fail, or the raw output — go back to the assistant, not just a green checkmark.</p>
        <div class="call">marshal.run_tests()</div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">04</div>
        <h3>Deploy</h3>
        <p>On a passing run, Marshal ships to the configured target. Anything short of green holds for your review instead of shipping anyway.</p>
        <div class="call">marshal.deploy(target)</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

